          "request": {
            "name": "Amazon Config Put Stored Query",
            "description": {
              "content": "<p>Saves a new query or updates an existing saved query. The <code>QueryName</code> must be unique for a single Amazon Web Services account and a single Amazon Web Services Region. You can create upto 300 queries in a single Amazon Web Services account and a single Amazon Web Services Region.</p> <note> <p> <code>PutStoredQuery</code> is an idempotent API. Subsequent requests won’t create a duplicate resource if one was already created. If a following request has different <code>tags</code> values, Config will ignore these differences and treat it as an idempotent request of the previous. In this case, <code>tags</code> will not be updated, even if they are different.</p> </note>",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
